---
import LessonPage from "../../../components/lesson/LessonPage.astro";
import { defineLesson } from "../../../data/lesson-schema.mjs";
export const page = defineLesson({
  "title": "Colors and basic adjectives · A0 Vocabulary · Curriculum Map",
  "slug": "colours-and-basic-adjectives",
  "level": "A0",
  "topic": "Colours & basic adjectives",
  "category": "Vocabulary & Topics",
  "contentType": "vocabulary",
  "status": "ready",
  "description": "Describe the things around you. A color or a quality word is an adjective : red , new , big . In English the adjective goes before the noun — a red car , not a car red — or after t",
  "sequence": 12,
  "prerequisites": [],
  "related": [],
  "assessments": [
    "a0-exit"
  ]
});
---
<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Vocabulary · Lesson 12</p>
  <h1>Colors &amp; basic <em>adjectives</em></h1>
  <p class="standfirst">Describe the things around you. A color or a quality word is an <strong>adjective</strong>: <span class="ex">red</span>, <span class="ex">new</span>, <span class="ex">big</span>. In English the adjective goes <strong>before</strong> the noun — <span class="ex">a red car</span>, not <span class="ex">a car red</span> — or <strong>after</strong> the verb <em>be</em>: <span class="ex">The car is red.</span></p>
  <div class="meta-row">
    <span class="tag">≈ 45–55 min</span>
    <span class="tag">colors</span>
    <span class="tag">opposites</span>
    <span class="tag">word order</span>
    <span class="tag">9 interactive tasks</span>
  </div>

  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow">
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Notice</b><span>Adjective before the noun.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Discover</b><span>Two places: before the noun, after be.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Match opposites, choose, and build.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Use</b><span>Describe your phone, car, and city.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">An adjective in English never adds <span class="ex">-s</span>. We say <span class="ex">two red cars</span>, never <span class="ex">two reds cars</span>. The noun can be plural; the adjective stays the same.</p>

  <h2>Notice before the rule</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Two phrases — one is right</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">a red car &nbsp; · &nbsp; a car red</span> &nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp;&nbsp; <span class="ex">The phone is new. &nbsp; · &nbsp; The new phone is.</span></p>
    <ul>
      <li>In <strong>a red car</strong>, where does the color word go — <strong>before</strong> or <strong>after</strong> the thing (the car)?</li>
      <li>In <strong>The phone is new</strong>, the adjective comes after one short word. Which word is it?</li>
      <li>So an adjective lives in two homes: right <strong>before a noun</strong>, or right <strong>after <em>be</em></strong>. Which two phrases above sound wrong to you?</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Discovery check — choose the color the cue describes</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">The hint in brackets describes the color of a real object</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="red">red</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="blue">blue</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="green">green</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="white">white</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="black">black</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The grass in the park is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="green" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(the color of grass)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>A clear sky in summer is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="blue" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(the color of the sky)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>Fresh snow is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="white" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(the color of snow)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>A stop sign on the street is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="red" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(the color of a stop sign)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>Coffee with no milk is almost <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="black" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(the color of dark coffee)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>The words: colors and opposites</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>Common colors for describing things around you. Each panel shows the real color:</p>
  <div class="swatch-grid" aria-label="Color swatches">
    <div class="swatch"><span class="sw" style="background:#E03131" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="nm">red</span></div>
    <div class="swatch"><span class="sw" style="background:#1971C2" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="nm">blue</span></div>
    <div class="swatch"><span class="sw" style="background:#2F9E44" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="nm">green</span></div>
    <div class="swatch"><span class="sw" style="background:#F2C200" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="nm">yellow</span></div>
    <div class="swatch"><span class="sw" style="background:#111111" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="nm">black</span></div>
    <div class="swatch"><span class="sw" style="background:#FFFFFF" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="nm">white</span></div>
    <div class="swatch"><span class="sw" style="background:#868E96" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="nm">gray</span></div>
    <div class="swatch"><span class="sw" style="background:#8B5E34" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="nm">brown</span></div>
    <div class="swatch"><span class="sw" style="background:#F76707" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="nm">orange</span></div>
    <div class="swatch"><span class="sw" style="background:#F06595" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="nm">pink</span></div>
    <div class="swatch"><span class="sw" style="background:#7048E8" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="nm">purple</span></div>
    <div class="swatch"><span class="sw" style="background:#4DABF7" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="nm">light blue</span></div>
    <div class="swatch"><span class="sw" style="background:#1864AB" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="nm">dark blue</span></div>
    <div class="swatch"><span class="sw" style="background:#15AABF" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="nm">turquoise</span></div>
    <div class="swatch"><span class="sw" style="background:#C9A227" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="nm">gold</span></div>
    <div class="swatch"><span class="sw" style="background:#CED4DA" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="nm">silver</span></div>
    <div class="swatch"><span class="sw" style="background:#D8C9A3" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="nm">beige</span></div>
    <div class="swatch"><span class="sw" style="background:#842029" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="nm">maroon</span></div>
  </div>

  <div class="lead-rule" style="margin-top:2.4rem"></div>
  <p>Now add seven common quality words. Each one has an opposite:</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>adjective</th><th>opposite</th><th>example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><b>big</b></td><td><b>small</b></td><td><span class="contraction">a big office · a small phone</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>new</b></td><td><b>old</b></td><td><span class="contraction">a new car · an old jacket</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>hot</b></td><td><b>cold</b></td><td><span class="contraction">hot coffee · cold water</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>good</b></td><td><b>bad</b></td><td><span class="contraction">a good idea · a bad day</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>long</b></td><td><b>short</b></td><td><span class="contraction">a long street · a short walk</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>cheap</b></td><td><b>expensive</b></td><td><span class="contraction">a cheap bag · an expensive watch</span></td></tr>
      <tr><td><b>fast</b></td><td><b>slow</b></td><td><span class="contraction">a fast train · a slow bus</span></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="note">
    <h3>Two rules to keep</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Before the noun:</strong> the adjective goes first. <span class="ex">a red car</span>, <span class="ex">a big office</span>, <span class="ex">a new phone</span> — never <span class="ex">a car red</span>.</li>
      <li><strong>After <em>be</em>:</strong> <span class="ex">The car is red. My phone is new. The coffee is hot.</span></li>
      <li><strong>No <em>-s</em> on the adjective:</strong> <span class="ex">two red cars</span>, never <span class="ex">two reds cars</span>.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <h2>Match the opposites</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-game>
    <h3>Drill 1 — match each word to its opposite</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Tap a word, then tap the opposite that fits it</p>
    <div class="tile-bank">
      <button class="tile" data-tile="small">small</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="old">old</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="cold">cold</button>
      <button class="tile" data-tile="expensive">expensive</button>
    </div>
    <div class="slot-board">
      <button class="slot" data-slot="small" data-placeholder="opposite of big">opposite of big</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="old" data-placeholder="opposite of new">opposite of new</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="cold" data-placeholder="opposite of hot">opposite of hot</button>
      <button class="slot" data-slot="expensive" data-placeholder="opposite of cheap">opposite of cheap</button>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-tiles>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-tiles>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Choose the quality word</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>

  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill>
    <h3>Drill 2 — choose the adjective the cue describes</h3>
    <p class="choice-hint">The hint in brackets points to one clear answer</p>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Answer choices">
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="big">big</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="new">new</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="hot">hot</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="expensive">expensive</button>
      <button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="fast">fast</button>
    </div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>I bought this phone yesterday, so it is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="new" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(not old)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The watch costs $900, so it is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="expensive" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(not cheap)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The coffee just came off the machine, so it is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="hot" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(not cold)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Our office has forty rooms, so it is very <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="big" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(not small)</span></span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The express train reaches the city in ten minutes, so it is <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="fast" data-placeholder="choose">choose</button>. &nbsp;<span class="contraction">(not slow)</span></span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Word order: put the adjective in its home</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>When you stack two adjectives, the order is <strong>size or opinion + color + noun</strong>: <span class="ex">a small black notebook</span>, <span class="ex">a big red car</span>. Build these aloud after you finish each one.</p>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="a small black notebook">
    <h3>Drill 3 — build the phrase</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">A notebook on your desk: small, and black. Build the phrase, then say it.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="black">black</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="a">a</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="notebook">notebook</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="small">small</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="the office is big">
    <h3>Drill 4 — build with <em>be</em></h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Now put the adjective after <em>be</em>. The office is large. Build the sentence.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="big">big</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="the">The</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="is">is</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="office">office</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-game" data-tile-builder data-answer="i have a new phone">
    <h3>Drill 5 — build the sentence</h3>
    <p class="tile-target">Talk about your phone: it is new. Build the sentence, then say it.</p>
    <div class="tile-bank" data-build-bank>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="phone">phone</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="i">I</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="new">new</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="have">have</button>
      <button class="tile" data-build-tile="a">a</button>
    </div>
    <div class="build-area" data-build-area data-placeholder="Tap words in order"></div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-build>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-build>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice and repair errors</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="red" data-fix="a red car" data-why="The adjective goes before the noun, so red comes before car: a red car, not a car red.">
    <h3>Drill 6 — fix the word order</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is in the wrong place.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="a">a</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="car">car</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="red">red</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="greens" data-fix="two green doors" data-why="An adjective never takes -s. The noun is plural (doors), but the adjective stays green, not greens.">
    <h3>Drill 7 — fix the adjective</h3>
    <p>Tap the word that is wrong.</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="two">two</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="greens">greens</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="doors">doors</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform>
    <h3>Drill 8 — fix the order, then say it</h3>
    <p>Say the correct phrase or sentence aloud first. Reveal only after you answer.</p>
    <div class="transform-list">
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> a bag blue &nbsp;→&nbsp; put the color in order</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>a blue bag</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> a watch expensive &nbsp;→&nbsp; put it in order</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>an expensive watch</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>3</b> The is car new. &nbsp;→&nbsp; fix the sentence</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>The car is new.</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>4</b> two whites shirts &nbsp;→&nbsp; remove the wrong -s</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>two white shirts</strong></p>
      </div>
      <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item>
        <p class="transform-cue"><b>5</b> a notebook small black &nbsp;→&nbsp; size + color + noun</p>
        <button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button>
        <p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>a small black notebook</strong></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Read and choose</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>A new office</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">“My new office is nice. The walls are white and the door is brown. I have a big black desk and two green chairs. My favorite thing is the small red lamp.”</span></p>
  </div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Good reading. You understood colors in a real description.">
    <h3>Read, then choose</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="white">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. What color are the walls?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="white">white</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="brown">brown</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="black">black</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="two">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. How many green chairs are there?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="two">two</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="one">one</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="three">three</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="the lamp">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. What is red?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the lamp">the lamp</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the desk">the desk</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="the door">the door</button></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="drill-actions">
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button>
      <button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button>
    </div>
    <p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Use it in real life</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Your phone:</b> Describe the phone in your hand. <span class="ex">My phone is black. It is new. It is a good phone.</span> Use a color and one quality word.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Your car or your bike:</b> Say two things about it. <span class="ex">My car is white. It is small and fast.</span> If you have no car, describe a bus or train you take.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Your clothes today:</b> Look down and name three things you are wearing. <span class="ex">I have a blue shirt, black shoes, and a brown jacket.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Your office or home:</b> Describe one room. <span class="ex">My office is big. The chairs are gray. The desk is old.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Your city:</b> Tell the teacher about your city with adjectives. <span class="ex">My city is big and expensive. The buses are slow. The parks are green.</span></div>

  <h2>Reflect</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Explain the choice</h3>
    <p>Complete this aloud: “An adjective goes ______ the noun, like <strong>a ____ car</strong>. It also comes after the word ______, like <strong>The car is ____</strong>. An adjective never adds ______, so I say <strong>two red cars</strong>.”</p>
    <p>Then say one true sentence about something <strong>near</strong> you using a color, and one using a quality word like <em>big</em>, <em>new</em>, or <em>good</em>.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Great. You can place an adjective before a noun and after be, and you know the colors and common opposites.">
    <h3>Final quiz — colors, opposites, and word order</h3>
    <div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="a red car">
        <p class="quiz-question">1. Which phrase is correct?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a red car">a red car</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a car red">a car red</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="a reds car">a reds car</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="old">
        <p class="quiz-question">2. What is the opposite of <em>new</em>?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="old">old</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="small">small</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="cold">cold</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="two green doors">
        <p class="quiz-question">3. Which is correct?</p>
        <div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="two green doors">two green doors</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="two greens doors">two greens doors</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="two door greens">two door greens</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="expensive">
        <p class="quiz-question">4. The watch costs $900. It is ___.</p>
